WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.405
Calling input inside a million-line loop adds per-line overhead in Python.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:10.736
Reading from sys.stdin buffers the stream and keeps I/O time predictable.

00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:14.680
Use a token iterator when numbers span multiple lines.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.703
Printing inside a tight multi-test loop flushes the output stream repeatedly.

00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:24.283
Collect formatted answers in a list and join them with newlines at the end.

00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:27.520
Single-pass output avoids hidden time limit failures.

00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:33.835
Before writing code, translate the maximum input size into an operation budget.

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:40.671
Two hundred thousand elements require linear or log-linear time to pass within one second.

00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:45.153
Reject quadratic ideas immediately when the bound is large.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:52.116
Isolate each test case inside a dedicated solve function so local variables stay fast and clean.

00:00:52.116 --> 00:00:56.341
Reset per-case state explicitly before reading the next test.

00:00:56.341 --> 00:01:00.358
Test single-element and boundary inputs before submitting.
